A Free organization of your own: one owned at a time.
MCP ACCESS
Set it up without the plugin →
Sign Claude Code in with your browser; it acts as you, in one of your organizations at a time. Connections you approve as @test-member show up here.
Install the Trov plugin in Claude Code:
/plugin marketplace add AndresL230/trov
/plugin install trov@trov
Run /mcp, choose trov, then Authenticate.
Your browser opens Trov. Choose how the connection picks an organization (you're in Test Free now), then click Allow — it shows up under Connected apps.
One connection covers all your organizations. When you allow it you choose how it picks one: follow the repository you are working in, or the organizations you tick, one at a time. You can change that later in Settings. Not using Claude Code? Claude on the 

